>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `augment_aesop`

``` hol4
aesopLib.augment_aesop :
  {name : string, phase : aesopLib.rphase,
   tactic : NTactical.ntactic} -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Registers a session-local tactic rule for Aesop.

`augment_aesop {name, phase, tactic}` appends an unindexed rule, so Aesop
offers it on every goal in its phase. The available phases are:

| Phase | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `aesopRule.RNorm k` | normalisation with integer penalty `k` |
| `aesopRule.RSafe` | deterministic safe reasoning |
| `aesopRule.RUnsafe n` | unsafe search with success percentage `n` |

An unsafe percentage must be from 1 through 100. Lower normalisation
penalties run first.

A tactic rule operates on a rendered HOL goal in which engine
metavariables are rigid. It therefore cannot create or assign engine
metavariables. A no-op result is rejected. Normalisation rules must close
the goal or return exactly one subgoal, and safe rules are committed only
when their application is deterministic.

The registration affects subsequent Aesop calls in the current session.
It is not stored in a theory and is not exported.

### Failure

Registration itself only records the rule. Errors or unsuitable results
from `tactic`, and an invalid unsafe percentage, are encountered when
Aesop tries the rule.

### Example

``` hol4
val _ =
  aesopLib.augment_aesop
    {name = "strip-conjunction",
     phase = aesopRule.RSafe,
     tactic = NTactical.LIFT (REPEAT CONJ_TAC)};
```

